        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(plugin-sdk): expose reply-session conflict classifier",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nPlugin authors and channel extensions currently duplicate reply-session initialization conflict classification using ad hoc regex and manual error.message checks. Without a shared, stable classifier, any change to the error message breaks hard-to-find classification logic across Discord, Signal, Slack, Telegram, and WhatsApp. The Plugin SDK should expose a single predicate that extensions import and trust.\n\n## Summary\n\n- expose `isReplySessionInitConflictError(error: unknown)` through\n  `openclaw/plugin-sdk/error-runtime`;\n- move the conflict error identity into a lightweight shared module;\n- replace duplicated classification logic in Discord, Signal, Slack,\n  Telegram, and WhatsApp;\n- update the Plugin SDK API baseline, surface budget, and subpath docs.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThe shared predicate recognizes:\n\n- `ReplySessionInitConflictError` instances;\n- strictly matched legacy conflict messages;\n- raw legacy message strings;\n- wrapped conflicts in `cause` and `error` chains;\n- compatible error-like objects with an exact message.\n\nIt intentionally does not classify name-only or partial-message matches.\n\nThis normalizes wrapped-error handling and strict message matching across\nchannels. Retry counts, backoff, terminal behavior, and user-facing messages\nare unchanged (Discord retry was already removed upstream; wrapping now\ncorrectly routes to terminal notice).\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n\n- classifier tests: 25/25 (typed error, legacy message, raw string,\n  cause-chain wrapping, error-like objects, no-throw contract, Proxy traps);\n- Plugin SDK export-contract tests: 6/6;\n- Discord: 138/138 (includes new wrapped-conflict test);\n- Signal: 7/7;\n- Slack: 13/13;\n- WhatsApp: 54/54;\n- Telegram: 115/118 (3 pre-existing Windows path-separator failures).\n\n### Static checks\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` — ✅;\n- `pnpm check:test-types` — ✅;\n- `pnpm build:plugin-sdk:strict-smoke` — ✅ (4/4 exports);\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check` — ✅;\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:surface:check` — ✅ (8150 public / 4534 callable);\n- `pnpm deadcode:knip` — ✅;\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` — ✅;\n- `pnpm check:import-cycles` — 0 cycles;\n- `pnpm check:madge-import-cycles` — 0 cycles;\n- `npx oxfmt --check` — 15 files correct;\n- `git diff --check` — clean.\n\nFour unrelated Windows-only failures were reproduced unchanged on the\nupstream/main baseline: one SQLite EBUSY cleanup failure and three Telegram\npath-separator assertions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- no retry or backoff changes;\n- no terminal-notice changes;\n- no new error code;\n- no changes to PR #108899;\n- QQBot migration is deferred until #108899 is merged.",
